{"id": "coin-change", "title": "Coin Change", "difficulty": "medium", "tags": ["dynamic-programming"], "statement": "coins is a list of distinct positive coin values, and you have unlimited coins of each value. Return the fewest coins needed to make exactly amount, or -1 if it is impossible. amount 0 needs 0 coins.\n\nExample: coins = [1,2,5], amount = 11 -> 3 (5+5+1)\nExample: coins = [2], amount = 3 -> -1", "entry": "coin_change", "starter": "def coin_change(coins, amount):\n    pass\n", "tests": [{"args": [[1, 2, 5], 11], "expected": 3}, {"args": [[2], 3], "expected": -1}, {"args": [[1], 0], "expected": 0}, {"args": [[9, 8], 0], "expected": 0, "n": 0}, {"args": [[6], 1], "expected": -1, "n": 1}, {"args": [[6, 11, 3, 2], 2], "expected": 1, "n": 2}, {"args": [[2, 1, 10], 3], "expected": 2, "n": 3}, {"args": [[5, 3], 5], "expected": 1, "n": 5}, {"args": [[4, 3], 8], "expected": 2, "n": 8}, {"args": [[7, 6, 9, 11], 13], "expected": 2, "n": 13}, {"args": [[10], 20], "expected": 2, "n": 20}, {"args": [[6, 3, 10, 2], 50], "expected": 5, "n": 50}, {"args": [[6, 8], 100], "expected": 13, "n": 100}, {"args": [[6, 4, 9, 3], 150], "expected": 17, "n": 150}, {"args": [[3, 5], 200], "expected": 40, "n": 200}]}